<title>BELGIUM: Boeing chief expects EU to clear McDonnell deal.</title>
<headline>Boeing chief expects EU to clear McDonnell deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing chief executive officer Phil Condit said on Tuesday he did not expect his company's alliance with McDonnell Douglas to cause any competition problems with the European Commission.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't expect any particular issues (from the Commission) out of this,&quot; he told a conference organised by the European Aviation Club.  </p>
<p>The Commission has already said that it has concerns about the deal's potential to create a dominant position in the European market over which it has jurisdiction.</p>
<p>Condit was to meet EU Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert later on Tuesday (approx 1430 GMT)</p>
<p>- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287-6830</p>
